    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0699" n="685" xml:id="pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.24/9–644</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Chief of the Division of North
                        and West Coast Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lyon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Director of
                        the Office of American Republic Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-06">September 6, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The underlying memorandum<anchor n="39" xml:id="d653-f1"/> indicates that Chile
                    has received in equipment about one-tenth of the Lend-Lease credit extended to
                    her (approximately $5,500,000 out of $50,000,000). I recommend that we agree
                    with Colonel Meals’<anchor n="40" xml:id="d653-f2"/> suggestion and let Chile
                    have a little material now. I think this will be beneficial from the point of
                    view of: <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Chilean-United States-Argentine relations.</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Keeping Chile satisfied until the Staff conferences are held. The
                            government (Chilean) officials will thus not be taken in by the
                            arguments which undoubtedly will be raised that Chile has been
                            completely deserted by the United States and should throw in her lot
                            with Argentina.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ecil</hi>] B. L[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">yon</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
